  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR Englis_Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 3,\n  \"section_title\": \"Grammar and Vocabulary (B2)\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 21,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct translation for 'It was suggested that we should apply for a grant'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) It had been suggested that we would apply.\",\n        \"B) It was advised that we could apply.\",\n        \"C) It was proposed that we should apply.\",\n        \"D) It had been suggested that we would apply.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 22,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence uses the passive voice correctly?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) The book was written by Jane Austen.\",\n        \"B) I wrote a book about Jane Austen's life.\",\n        \"C) A new theory has been proposed to explain this phenomenon.\",\n        \"D) The students were given an essay on their own work.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 23,\n      \"question\": \"Which advanced conditional sentence is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) If she had studied harder, they would have passed the exam.\",\n        \"B) They will be completed if we finish today.\",\n        \"C) She is going to visit her grandmother when she retires.\",\n        \"D) If they hadn't arrived on time, the meeting would have been cancelled.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 24,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following discourse markers is used correctly to connect two ideas?\"\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) In addition, I think that...\",\n        \"B) However, she didn't agree with me.\",\n        \"C) Therefore, we should continue the discussion.\",\n        \"D) As a result, I decided to change my mind.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 25,\n      \"question\": \"Which collocation is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) I have a meeting with the director.\",\n        \"B) He has an appointment for lunch today.\",\n        \"C) She is due a reward for her hard work.\",\n        \"D) We have a conference on Friday.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 26,\n      \"question\": \"Which dependent prepositional phrase is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) I will call you when I am finished.\",\n        \"B) She lives near the park because she loves walking there.\",\n        \"C) They work in a factory that manufactures toys.\",\n        \"D) I will send you an email when it is ready.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 27,\n      \"question\": \"Which precise lexical choice is appropriate for the sentence?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) I am confident that he will succeed.\",\n        \"B) She feels uncomfortable in this position.\",\n        \"C) He is quite anxious about the exam results.\",\n        \"D) They were surprised by her decision.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 28,\n      \"question\": \"Which reported speech is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) He said that he would go to the party.\",\n        \"B) They suggested that we should not attend it.\",\n        \"C) She implied that she wasn't interested.\",\n        \"D) We were told to leave the building.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 29,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence uses the correct dependent preposition?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) I will meet her at the station.\",\n        \"B) She is expected to arrive by midnight.\",\n        \"C) They are waiting for him in the corner.\",\n        \"D) We have finished our tasks.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 30,\n      \"question\": \"Which verb phrase is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) I am going to the store.\",\n        \"B) They have been working on this project for months.\",\n        \"C) She was reading a book when she got called out of class.\",\n        \"D) We are prepared to discuss the issue.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    }\n}\n```",
